(0,0),$ $(6,-12).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-147611/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-147611"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-21063"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/6501b1a7e9429c786905c11835410111c32ac0337f1ba63bff130d327350316c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(6,3)$, $(8,4)$ and $(10,5).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/a91af151d3dc0e48aef0eef58012f6c9f72aaff02aafae2d55fe0714c29c96e3.png)" :db/ensure [:question/valid