 [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97021/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0710a7e7-2fa9-5968-9699-25053d9a320b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97021/selection/bd35eee5075e82746869319a38e65eb06ff076e5befc4d3df88f6736bac1e6a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-97021/selection/b522fe70d0b4ddf97ed8f538c279fb16e9634b5c2db645cada43e83810994446" "q-97021/selection/7fc44e3cc1f777f30efe55165f745916d43ea2225d649743b8b41315dfb17a2d" "q-97021/selection/bd35eee5075e82746869319a38e65eb06ff076e5befc4d3df88f6736bac1e6a2" "q-97021/selection/56143d8192a140db7ee41a9cef5e62835669f8c28169d68726f73607fb50f135" "q-97021/selection/f14efec9323ccbbbc8852a44dc013617fcccb11d8658e5f7b3d5d282658a26f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97021" :question/id #uuid "de81ae6d-990c-555a-8180-3e9f001332f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97021" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/6724aca14f79c6df70d7bdfca41dc03fb448ae5566d05a5ee9c96dc6cf505812.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,2)$, $(5,-10),$ $(-2,4).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/e7bfe2b85983b2cd45dd3e2f9bbfeed0d8440d838ae11fa4afb0b0b1476529ea.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97021/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-21061"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-147649"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/57941a3ed467617de9d41a2d8239b75060ba90b7a8c8980e5dabd3afb0be8b6b.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(-5,5),$ $(-3,3).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/cf336b4522756131aeb6dd9bc48ada6f8b255526b6ae20120dcf40f155b1b95c.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162206"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/e6d0ce147aec90c3840a893e36596fbadf981ff96559f65d055f4486406cca7f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162202"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/8978d3bb02b4032b6e3a8b4a85878db647eb8323ac5b0423b5a9a6fab121c7e7.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162207"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/57948af956c9b83ed944fafc26e81a5c003401f753bc520e088ffdbd71915c3a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203/selection/4b7649d656eb4e6f40e81460f6b84b104149aace596473d883fc9f11ea628ebc" :answer/id #uuid "d115ee20-9dda-513b-9aed-4624b6734666" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rectangle" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203/selection/a46b9d9cb098f30c2bfb1712d5eac34a9a6a7683788497e7234aec27f048077a" :answer/id #uuid "1de74d72-127e-556b-8427-6d9364d48054" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A pentagon" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203/selection/c2d1a5ac4ed1170ec4ba684e8dd01cdba007525d6370ddfd38066ec585122318" :answer/id #uuid "099e2f87-23cd-5617-9b1a-dd2d77f75d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A line segment" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203/selection/0f01227ab4132a1cf25abe47ace21e46fc0c901af076ff4c5dae675af9c522e9" :answer/id #uuid "ec42bf66-f144-51df-9408-97d76dbc5561" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203/selection/f5b2bfafb2dc92d309ddb5e86bc50a427805dfd590fef68751ff0eb644197542" :answer/id #uuid "9274fb24-d9f8-5683-9c48-c7c8265f0645" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A point, different from the origin" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb7c053-b2bf-547a-a46c-df87d98b946f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162203/selection/c2d1a5ac4ed1170ec4ba684e8dd01cdba007525d6370ddfd38066ec585122318" :answer-field/choices ["q-162203/selection/4b7649d656eb4e6f40e81460f6b84b104149aace596473d883fc9f11ea628ebc" "q-162203/selection/a46b9d9cb098f30c2bfb1712d5eac34a9a6a7683788497e7234aec27f048077a" "q-162203/selection/c2d1a5ac4ed1170ec4ba684e8dd01cdba007525d6370ddfd38066ec585122318" "q-162203/selection/0f01227ab4132a1cf25abe47ace21e46fc0c901af076ff4c5dae675af9c522e9" "q-162203/selection/f5b2bfafb2dc92d309ddb5e86bc50a427805dfd590fef68751ff0eb644197542"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162203" :question/id #uuid "ec7f25ec-c53e-5db0-8670-17fbf89adc9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-162203" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/bfbd80c4e052ae3c286d25b2cd7bf5a1ffcd76ac5a030b7f9b633d0f12517231.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the pentagon shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 9-6\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a singular nonzero matrix. Therefore, the image of the pentagon under the action of $T$ is a line segment." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162203/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fea43b6-fd7b-5edc-b6b7-7f8b2cbab502"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162203"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-162208"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/0231cc5aaf661cc873f18ff676a03d66927be48b49d38649efc45860197d18c1.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12423"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/3ff8dc37a532cfe49a2fbd8c02a1b27c50642d8e4c54def6984f3596f68065fa.png)\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,2), (0,1)$ and $(1,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of $S',$ the image of $S$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$\n\n- $(-2,0)$\n\n- $(0,0)$\n\n- $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12424"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/5414050f8a5a5208b4424333e947919ce196687f8bfb0e60c2ced0a04a2695cc.png)  Find the image of the triangle shown below under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/853fd7d5c09944a5bacd0c2b3453504f3fa1eea9d8d3b2c3bdd4f0f44889dc16.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/95c80fe2654c8f6eb4b65492eab1efb07f568375b2960b1633e5e2e1a7741a8b.png)\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6), (1,-2),$ and $(-2,4).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/3fd1073b2eaa5aa9c21e537fcc4dc6cf538ab2992c0732f64da50dbcb63d8fd4.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12438"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/89efcd0ecb51dac08a1102c5a347eea3459f7209de7cbac0a88b192259ca3b7e.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/501ab476f0e420892fee6c87307dd33f260affc1533019621b366b5462920322.png)\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
